<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- The Vacuum kit (Hunter x Hunter, Shizuku's Blinky): a wand with a floor head, held as a blunt
       melee weapon. On each cast a canister with a face rises out of the floor beside the holder and
       sinks back after; between casts only the wand is held. Rules agreed 2026-09-25; the numbers are
       placeholders from the sketches (Tools/VfxLab/web/sketches/vacuum-*.js, lib/vacuum.js) and every
       one is a field here or in AG_Vacuum_Abilities.xml.

       Mouth and stomach: the mouth holds one real thing, the last swallowed, which Spit fires. When
       something new comes in, what was in the mouth is destroyed and its kg go to the stomach, a
       weight only. Fullness = mouth + stomach, at most capacityKg. The holder is slowed by slowPerKg
       per kg (AG_VacuumFull), never under minMoveFactor. It is all kept on the weapon: a dropped or
       handed-over vacuum keeps its contents, nothing spills when the holder dies, and the mouth's
       thing is lost if the weapon is destroyed.

       The comps are listed with Inherit="False" because CompProperties_Vacuum is the weapon's
       CompEquippable (its fullness readout is an equipped gizmo), as the flame gauntlet's is.
       BaseWeapon's other two comps are repeated here; if BaseWeapon gains one, add it. Not
       smeltable: it has no cost to give back, like the water gun. No weaponTags, so raiders never
       carry it. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseWeapon">
    <defName>AG_Vacuum</defName>
    <label>vacuum</label>
    <description>The wand and floor head of a conjured vacuum cleaner. When it is used, a squat canister with a face rises out of the floor beside the wielder, unwinds its hose to the wand, and sinks back when it is done. In melee the wand is a blunt club.\n\nWhile it is equipped, the wielder can use Suck, Spit and Digest.\n\nSuck takes every loose item and all filth within 2 tiles of a spot up to 12 tiles away, and the weapon out of the hands of the nearest hostile there. Spit fires the last thing swallowed back out: 1.5 blunt damage per kg, at most 40, and it lands as itself. Digest destroys everything inside.\n\nThe mouth holds only the last thing swallowed; anything older is in the stomach for good. The vacuum holds 100 kg, and the wielder moves 0.4% slower for every kg inside.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>RimArt/Vacuum/Vacuum</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <smeltable>false</smeltable>
    <relicChance>0</relicChance>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>WeaponsMelee</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <weaponClasses>
      <li>Melee</li>
    </weaponClasses>
    <tradeability>All</tradeability>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>400</MarketValue>
      <Mass>2.5</Mass>
      <MaxHitPoints>120</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>1</DeteriorationRate>
      <Beauty>0</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <comps Inherit="False">
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_Vacuum">
        <capacityKg>100</capacityKg>
        <slowPerKg>0.004</slowPerKg>
        <minMoveFactor>0.1</minMoveFactor>
        <abilities>
          <li>AG_Vacuum_Suck</li>
          <li>AG_Vacuum_Spit</li>
          <li>AG_Vacuum_Digest</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Forbiddable"/>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Styleable"/>
    </comps>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities><li>Blunt</li></capacities>
        <power>9</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>wand</label>
        <capacities><li>Blunt</li></capacities>
        <power>7</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.8</cooldownTime>
      </li>
    </tools>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
